Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"e2b9b1f1-fbca-eb44-ba0c-82b704d09c8c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8a31bac7-763a-7542-95c0-c8d026bca7df"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"40665e0f-3a51-3e46-8b37-1f4adf2dbfb0"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"a97c303b-d0ab-8146-ada0-253d30f2ccb0"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dd34f90c-7b9c-4145-85b2-ee4f4fc0406c"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ddc58793-df85-d742-bd5e-1af59cec393c"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"32d03f95-3210-8445-9fc3-35b35a1d23ff"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b25e7fe4-3181-b944-8856-b8e2254c3330"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"0da59627-4d44-2a44-a833-25ab18312f92"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"06995205-5e8f-3547-b272-e55c5d97a583"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"778d87da-39bb-e145-b83d-268cd62dbc6d"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"d5838d29-83b2-e943-8009-483b964ac788"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f4416d25-e87f-c049-8973-c6e3ebde9a2c"],

